| What is the main purpose of an API? | An API (Application Programming Interface) allows different software applications to communicate, exchange data, and interact with each other safely. |
| What is the difference between symmetric and asymmetric encryption? | Symmetric encryption uses a single key to both encrypt and decrypt data, while asymmetric encryption uses a public key to encrypt data and a separate private key to decrypt it. |
| What does a 404 HTTP status code mean? | A 404 status code indicates that the server could not find the requested web page or resource. |
| Why are environment variables used instead of hardcoding values? | Environment variables isolate sensitive configuration data (like API keys and database passwords) from the application source code, preventing accidental leaks. |
| What is the role of a reverse proxy? | A reverse proxy sits in front of web servers, routing client requests to the appropriate backend server to assist with load balancing, caching, and security encryption. |
| What is Docker used for? | Docker is a containerization platform that packages an application and all its dependencies into a single container, ensuring it runs consistently across different environments. |
